From 37332ffb0b8d1d45921e3bd4b296ff0fc107fec3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:06:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(catalog): a catalog case can expect a refusal

case.toml `expect` takes "post" or "refusal". A refusal case has no
<case>.nc. Its script saves the project and then runs the refused step
without a catch. refusal.txt holds the refusal lines that the script host
records, byte for byte.

- The app catalog tests compare the recorded lines with refusal.txt. A
  refusal case that posts, or a changed refusal text, fails them.
- `cargo xtask catalog --check` accepts a refusal case without a .nc and
  compares its lines. `cargo xtask catalog` writes refusal.txt.
- The 12 existing cases change to expect = "post".
- New case 2d/drill-overfeed: a Drill above its tool's rated feed (#2598).

Stacked on #3139.

Fixes #2856

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
